<title>INDIA: Indian soy prices in steady gains on low arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soy prices in steady gains on low arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices on Thursday continued steady at higher levels on poor arrivals and some markets closed for a local festival, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil refined fell by 100 rupees per tonne on increased selling on poor demand. Soyoil solvent was steady, the said.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction reached record levels.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was $282-285 per tonne in extraction. Rapeseed extraction was $117-118 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 3,900-4,000 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 3,900-3,950 FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
